; === Zyl Standard Library — Compiler local-closure inlining (retired) ===
; Module: compiler/closure_inline
;
; This pass used to beta-reduce `(let NAME (fn params body) LETBODY)`
; into LETBODY when NAME captured an enclosing variable and was only
; ever called directly -- a stopgap from before closures had a runtime
; representation, when ic-lambda (icnf.zyl) lowered any capturing
; lambda it could not prove safe to a useless (IConst 0).
;
; Closures are now real values (icnf.zyl's ic-lambda /
; ic-lambda-closure, codegen.zyl's cg-call-indirect), so the stopgap is
; no longer needed, and splicing a lambda body into its call sites is
; not hygienic in general (an argument expression can be captured by a
; parameter name, the body's free names can be shadowed at the call
; site). The pass is kept as an identity step so the pipeline's phase
; list and the bundle's file list stay as they are.

(use compiler/ast)
(use compiler/expr_inner)
(use compiler/icnf)

(defn ci-expand-program (_arena prog)
  prog)
